{
 "about": "Every delivery on which agenttrace/messages.py (A) and agenttrace/refcount.py (B) disagree after the last crosscheck run, grouped by cause, with a judgement of which side is right. Judged by reading samples of each group and by the hand-audit labels (agenttrace/claims/audited_links.json); not every row was read.",
 "tuning_rounds_of_the_reference": 1,
 "tuning_note": "The reference was written from docs/counting-rule.md and debugged on synthetic examples. It was then run once on all datasets (round 0: release 7 both / 16 only A / 418 only B; wiki 9111 / 756 / 180; demo, benign and the eight samples identical in deliveries). The disagreements were read once and the reference changed once (redaction markers with spaces inside a string, JSON-wrapped programs, shell pipes, LFS operations inside strings, R7 with an indexed name, assignments inside callbacks, grades of structural reads, the marker definition of R27). It was not changed again after the second run, except that its tie-break was set to the spec's (input order; with record-id order the wiki logs differ on 29 + 29 deliveries). Later the same day R17 got an exception (the quoted value of a config key, such as data_files: \"reference://...\" in a pasted dataset card, is not a held name); it was stated in docs/counting-rule.md and added to both implementations at once. That is a rule change, not a tuning round: the delivery sets of both sides on every dataset were the same before and after it (release 19 both / 4 only A / 173 only B).",
